      <p style="margin-bottom:20px;">Madison sits in the Tennessee Valley, where summer humidity regularly exceeds 85% and stays elevated from April through October. That sustained humidity doesn't just feel uncomfortable — it feeds mold growth in any space with limited airflow: crawlspaces, closets, behind appliances, inside HVAC systems. Homes with slab foundations on Madison's clay-heavy soil trap ground moisture against the foundation year-round. We inspect and remediate mold in Madison homes every month, not just after flood events — because the baseline humidity alone is sufficient to drive growth in improperly ventilated spaces.</p>
